{"name":"Rosy Sunset","hex":"#d95854","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Rose-coloured.","Of any reddish hue from bright pink to the color of ruddy cheeks in a light-skinned person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make pinkish in colour.","To present in a deceptively optimistic or positive light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosy"},{"term":"sunset","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The moment each evening when the sun disappears below the western horizon.","The changes in color of the sky before and after sunset."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunset"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosy","blocks":[{"text":"Rosy is a given name or nickname and, more rarely, a surname. It may refer to:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosy","wikidata":"Q56540504"},{"title":"Sunset","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset is the disappearance of the Sun at the end of the Sun path, below the horizon of the Earth due to its rotation. As viewed from everywhere on Earth, it is a phenomenon that happens approximately once every 24 hours, except in areas close to the poles. The equinox Sun sets due west at the moment of both the spring and autumn equinoxes. As viewed from the Northern Hemisphere, the Sun sets to the northwest in the spring and summer, and to the southwest in the autumn and winter; these seasons are reversed for the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg/330px-Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset","wikidata":"Q166564"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"},{"title":"Sunset (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color sunset is a pale tint of orange. It is a representation of the average color of clouds when the sunlight from a sunset is reflected from them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Sunset_2007-1.jpg/330px-Sunset_2007-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_(color)","wikidata":"Q11696368"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Cape_may.jpg/500px-Cape_may.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Cape_may.jpg/500px-Cape_may.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sunset over the Delaware Bay at Sunset Beach, New Jersey, U.S., seen through cirrus clouds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACape_may.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Fiery_sunset_clouds_over_city_silhouette.jpg/500px-Fiery_sunset_clouds_over_city_silhouette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Fiery_sunset_clouds_over_city_silhouette.jpg/1280px-Fiery_sunset_clouds_over_city_silhouette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Fiery_sunset_clouds_over_city_silhouette.jpg/500px-Fiery_sunset_clouds_over_city_silhouette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Intense red clouds cause